\title{mbiedesign: Model-based cancer screening trial design}
\description{
Model-based design of cancer screening trials that use late-stage cancer incidence as the endpoint. A calibrated multistate natural-history model, fit by maximum likelihood to population incidence data, is used to project stage-specific trial outcomes under the traditional and intended-effect (IE) designs, and to compute the per-arm sample size and relative efficiency of each design.
